+
+## Switch CPU foundation overlay (M02, 2026-11-08)
+
+The root Switch port keeps these changes in a maintained patch against the
+pinned checkout. The desktop defaults remain active unless stated otherwise.
+
+- `ps2_render_worker.cpp`: select the existing USE_SSE2NEON boundary rather
+  than unconditionally including x86 headers; preserve CSR transfer and waits.
+- `ps2_control.cpp`: parse the same 127.0.0.1 listener address with inet_pton
+  because libnx/newlib does not define INADDR_LOOPBACK; fail closed on error.
+- `ps2_runtime.cpp`: optional spike diagnostics report -1 when the host has
+  no CLOCK_THREAD_CPUTIME_ID, matching the existing unavailable Windows case.
+  Wall-clock values are never reported as thread CPU time.
+- `ps2_perf.cpp`: PS2X_HEADLESS excludes only ImGui drawing and overlay key
+  handling; counters, sampling, CSV and summaries remain compiled. This is a
+  CPU-test configuration, not an implementation of the game's UI.
+
+The Switch build also requests POSIX.1-2008 declarations for newlib fseeko;
+libc symbol inspection confirms that implementation exists. No dummy seek
+implementation or narrowed offset was added. Numeric/runtime execution proof
+remains required independently of compilation.
+
+The headless null RHI explicitly rejects UI initialization and never calls ImGui.
+The public test fixtures were reconciled with six already-documented runtime
+contracts: async stacks in 0x80000-0x100000, IOP heap from 0x80000, batched IOP
+progress, DIRECTHL-framed IMAGE continuations, and JR reading current VI. The
+pristine pin and initial overlay both failed the same six cases in accurate VU
+mode; original failures remain in root M02 evidence. No guest runtime arithmetic
+or control flow was changed to satisfy these fixture updates. JR source check:
+https://github.com/PCSX2/pcsx2/blob/master/pcsx2/VUops.cpp (_vuJR/_vuJALR).
+The JR fixture distinguishes old/new target and checks a single delay slot.
+
+M02 packed-accumulator audit additionally found that the inherited two-argument
+PMFHL helpers and PMTHL emission ignored hi1/lo1. The overlay now passes all four
+64-bit halves, selects words/halfwords explicitly, clamps SLW/SH at the correct
+signed widths, and preserves unaffected upper words on PMTHL. Scalar regression
+models distinguish both banks. Architectural cross-check: PCSX2 MMI.cpp PMFHL
+and PMTHL (https://github.com/PCSX2/pcsx2/blob/master/pcsx2/MMI.cpp). The original
+private generated EE contains zero uses of these helper calls; this is a CPU
+foundation correctness fix, not observed game behavior or a performance claim.
